Y2NzA4MDU5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:2d","name":"topic:2d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":16,"created_at":"2025-07-20T15:38:52Z","updated_at":"2025-08-07T22:35:13Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.4.1\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Nvidia RTX 4070 - intel i5 13600kf\n\n### Issue description\n\nAs you can see in the screenshots with the clip enabled (clip only as well as clip + draw) or disabled. the depiction of collision shapes is also clipped. I'd say this shouldn't happen since collision shapes are not part of standard visuals but rather serve to let the user know the bounds for the collisions (the collision itself is not clipped, only the collision shape).\nYou can imagine how this makes working with colliders difficult under these conditions :).\n\nDisabled\n<img width=\"1392\" height=\"1265\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5f852396-2b0d-420e-9ed7-b941e70eee84\" />\n\nClip Only\n<img width=\"1392\" height=\"1261\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7825b664-02fb-410b-8123-688a2a18775c\" />\n\nClip + Draw\n<img width=\"1392\" height=\"1258\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d888adbb-9ece-4ce5-849e-4fecf0248011\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Add ColorRect.\n2. Give the ColorRect a CollisionShape2D as a child.\n3. Set CircleShape2D as the Shape of the CollisionShape2D.\n4. On the ColorRect go to Visibility section in the Inspector and change Clip Children to Clip Only.\n5. Obsserve the debug shape is now limited only to the ColorRect area.\n\n(This is not ColorRect issue, I used it just as an example, other Control/Node2D nodes which have the Clip Children setting behave the same.)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A. If it's really needed I'll add a simple one but I can't do it right now, I'll be doing it later but it's simple to test if nothing else.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108800/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108800/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}